course: dictionary
lesson: 7503
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives potato two: a vegetable that grows under the ground, and a couch potato, which is a person who sits watching TV a lot. The words around it show which meaning is meant.
explain: «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak, fried leftover cabbage and potato.» The clues are dish, fried and cabbage, so potato is the vegetable you eat. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases do not mean what their words say. «He had just handed the meanness on, like a hot potato.» Nobody is holding a real potato. Hot potato means something passed quickly from one person to another, as you would drop something too hot to hold.
fact: A potato is a vegetable that grows under the ground, and we eat it cooked.
fact: In science, a potato is a tuber: a swollen underground stem that stores food, not a root.
fact: «Couch potato» means a person who sits watching TV a lot.
fact: From 1845 a potato disease destroyed Ireland's main food, and the Great Famine followed.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, the context tells you which one to use.
exercise: «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak, fried leftover cabbage and potato.» In this sentence, what is a potato? | A person who sits watching TV | A type of fish | A kind of sausage | *A vegetable that grows under the ground
exercise: «He had just handed the meanness on, like a hot potato.» What does hot potato mean here? | A very hot vegetable to eat | *Something passed quickly from one person to another | A cooking pot | A sunny day at the seaside
exercise: Which one is a couch potato? | A swollen stem that stores food | A vegetable grown under the ground | *A person who sits watching TV a lot | A pan for frying cabbage
test: In science, what is a potato? | *A swollen underground stem that stores food | A root | A type of seed | A leaf that grows in water
test: In science, what are the «eyes» of a potato? | Tiny seeds inside the flesh | Spots that show it is rotten | *Buds that can grow new plants | Small holes in the skin
exam: Tom says, «Stop being a couch potato and help me peel the potatoes!» What does couch potato mean here? | A vegetable grown under the ground | A kind of fried cabbage | *A person who sits watching TV a lot | A sofa made of potato sacks
